      "index": "bXo",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1086068274,
      "version": 38,
      "versionNonce": 1579184430,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1764349457941,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "🟦 3. What Happens When You Use Spring Boot Web?\n\nWhen you run your Spring Boot web app:\n\n@SprinBootApplication → starts Spring\n |\n |→ Creates Embedded Tomcat (port 8080)\n |\n |→ Registers DispatcherServlet\n |\n |→ Scans Controller classes\n |\n |→ Maps URLs (@GetMapping, @PostMapping)\n\n\nNow your browser can hit:\n\nhttp://localhost:8080/hello\n\n\nAnd Spring will forward the request to the correct controller.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "🟦 3. What Happens When You Use Spring Boot Web?\n\nWhen you run your Spring Boot web app:\n\n@SprinBootApplication → starts Spring\n |\n |→ Creates Embedded Tomcat (port 8080)\n |\n |→ Registers DispatcherServlet\n |\n |→ Scans Controller classes\n |\n |→ Maps URLs (@GetMapping, @PostMapping)\n\n\nNow your browser can hit:\n\nhttp://localhost:8080/hello\n\n\nAnd Spring will forward the request to the correct controller.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
