      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bYY",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1932265586,
      "version": 36,
      "versionNonce": 1023405678,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1764350783781,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "🔥 So WHY same word “Model” is used?\n\nBecause MVC architecture has 3 parts:\n\nModel → data to display\nView → front-end (JSP/HTML)\nController → handles request\n\n\nIn MVC, Model simply means “data that View needs”, not database.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "🔥 So WHY same word “Model” is used?\n\nBecause MVC architecture has 3 parts:\n\nModel → data to display\nView → front-end (JSP/HTML)\nController → handles request\n\n\nIn MVC, Model simply means “data that View needs”, not database.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
