    {
      "id": "iy8W6x9eNM1rjq00QPjUo",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 358.22767117534704,
      "y": 15304.901234197145,
      "width": 846.999755859375,
      "height": 70,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bYb",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 419810158,
      "version": 22,
      "versionNonce": 818365678,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1764350984105,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "But data inside the MVC Model can come from a database.\nlet's see how ",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "But data inside the MVC Model can come from a database.\nlet's see how ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "3NCko9c4Y_ojbtbB15yt_",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 377.3576860090716,
      "y": 15386.841201024255,
      "width": 966.1144732901414,
      "height": 675,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bYc",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 639566766,
      "version": 112,
      "versionNonce": 1729461554,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1764351037402,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "⭐ “Model in Spring MVC ≠ Database Model.”\n\nEven if the data originates from the DB, the purpose of the MVC Model is ONLY:\n\nTo carry data from Controller → JSP/HTML View\n\nLet’s break it fully.\n\n🟦 1. Yes — MVC Model CAN contain database data\n\nExample:\n\nStudent student = studentService.getStudentById(1);\nmodel.addAttribute(\"student\", student);\n\n\nHere:\n\n1.student was fetched from database ✔\n\n2.But you put it in model ONLY to send it to JSP ✔\n\n3.model does NOT save anything to the database ❌\n\n4.model is NOT part of ORM ❌\n\nSo data source can be DB, but model’s job is NOT database mapping, only view rendering.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "⭐ “Model in Spring MVC ≠ Database Model.”\n\nEven if the data originates from the DB, the purpose of the MVC Model is ONLY:\n\nTo carry data from Controller → JSP/HTML View\n\nLet’s break it fully.\n\n🟦 1. Yes — MVC Model CAN contain database data\n\nExample:\n\nStudent student = studentService.getStudentById(1);\nmodel.addAttribute(\"student\", student);\n\n\nHere:\n\n1.student was fetched from database ✔\n\n2.But you put it in model ONLY to send it to JSP ✔\n\n3.model does NOT save anything to the database ❌\n\n4.model is NOT part of ORM ❌\n\nSo data source can be DB, but model’s job is NOT database mapping, only view rendering.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
