    {
      "id": "PnJEL_BfFo57yfl8Xokyr",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 390.43931104381795,
      "y": 16623.867788061943,
      "width": 539,
      "height": 400,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bYg",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1339627890,
      "version": 39,
      "versionNonce": 1924979890,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1764351094771,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "🟥 2. Why MVC Model is NOT a database model\nBecause:\n\n-It does not know about tables\n\n-It does not know about SQL\n\n-It does not create/update/delete database rows\n\n-It exists only until the JSP is rendered\n\n-It is basically a map (key → value)\n\nUnder the hood, model behaves like:\n\nMap<String, Object> attributes = new HashMap<>();",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "🟥 2. Why MVC Model is NOT a database model\nBecause:\n\n-It does not know about tables\n\n-It does not know about SQL\n\n-It does not create/update/delete database rows\n\n-It exists only until the JSP is rendered\n\n-It is basically a map (key → value)\n\nUnder the hood, model behaves like:\n\nMap<String, Object> attributes = new HashMap<>();",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
