      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1764351155126,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "🟩 3. Database Model (Entity) is completely different\n\nExample:\n\n@Entity\npublic class Student {\n    @Id\n    private int id;\n    private String name;\n}\n\n\nThis is a database model because:\n\n-It is stored in database\n\n-Maps to a table student\n\n-Hibernate uses it\n\n-Spring Data JPA saves it\n\nThis model survives on disk (database).\nMVC Model does NOT.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "🟩 3. Database Model (Entity) is completely different\n\nExample:\n\n@Entity\npublic class Student {\n    @Id\n    private int id;\n    private String name;\n}\n\n\nThis is a database model because:\n\n-It is stored in database\n\n-Maps to a table student\n\n-Hibernate uses it\n\n-Spring Data JPA saves it\n\nThis model survives on disk (database).\nMVC Model does NOT.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
