      "seed": 579492334,
      "version": 23,
      "versionNonce": 1377957166,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1764360924168,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. If you want to map (use annotation called @RequestMapping(“/”) \n\n@Controller \npublic class HomeController{ \n@RequestMapping(“/”) \npublic String home(){ \nreturn \"index.jsp\"; \n} \n} \n\n\n2. Run  \n⇨ You get something to download.\n\n3. Why isn’t it working? \n⇨ By default, Spring Boot does not support JSP. \n⇨ Need dependency MVN Repository \nAs per the Tomcat version, use the Tomcat Jasper version.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. If you want to map (use annotation called @RequestMapping(“/”) \n\n@Controller \npublic class HomeController{ \n@RequestMapping(“/”) \npublic String home(){ \nreturn \"index.jsp\"; \n} \n} \n\n\n2. Run  \n⇨ You get something to download.\n\n3. Why isn’t it working? \n⇨ By default, Spring Boot does not support JSP. \n⇨ Need dependency MVN Repository \nAs per the Tomcat version, use the Tomcat Jasper version.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
