    {
      "id": "dTE1eYlTMG7FWN8NvPI3W",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 260.4006753261292,
      "y": 25164.714361069426,
      "width": 679.8968747531784,
      "height": 450,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bZI",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1638345838,
      "version": 89,
      "versionNonce": 1630826674,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1764395382095,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "🟦 1. What is a Servlet?\n\nA Servlet is a Java class that runs on a server and handles\nHTTP requests.\n\n✔ A Servlet can:\n\nTake input from the browser\n\nProcess the request\n\nGenerate HTML response\n\nSend the response back to the browser\n\n✔ Simplified:\n\nServlet = Java program that generates dynamic HTML.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "🟦 1. What is a Servlet?\n\nA Servlet is a Java class that runs on a server and handles HTTP requests.\n\n✔ A Servlet can:\n\nTake input from the browser\n\nProcess the request\n\nGenerate HTML response\n\nSend the response back to the browser\n\n✔ Simplified:\n\nServlet = Java program that generates dynamic HTML.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
