      "seed": 1088859118,
      "version": 57,
      "versionNonce": 1424570606,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1764395461285,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "🟦 2. What is JSP? (Java Server Page)\n\nJSP is basically an HTML file with Java code inside it.\n\nExample:\n\n<h1>Hello <%= name %></h1>\n\n\nYou mix:\n\n-HTML\n\n-CSS\n\n-Java expressions\n\n-Java loops\n\nJSP makes writing web pages easier than writing HTML inside Java\nstrings.\n\n✔ Simplified:\n\nJSP = HTML page + Java code.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "🟦 2. What is JSP? (Java Server Page)\n\nJSP is basically an HTML file with Java code inside it.\n\nExample:\n\n<h1>Hello <%= name %></h1>\n\n\nYou mix:\n\n-HTML\n\n-CSS\n\n-Java expressions\n\n-Java loops\n\nJSP makes writing web pages easier than writing HTML inside Java strings.\n\n✔ Simplified:\n\nJSP = HTML page + Java code.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
