      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1764395547057,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "🟦 3. Why do we need JSP if Servlets already exist?\n\nIf you write full HTML inside a Servlet, it becomes messy:\n\nout.println(\"<html>\");\nout.println(\"<body>\");\nout.println(\"<h1>Hello User</h1>\");\nout.println(\"</body></html>\");\n\n\nThis is extremely hard to maintain.\n\nSo JSP was created to make UI writing easier.\n\n✔ JSP = Best for HTML\n✔ Servlet = Best for logic / processing",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "🟦 3. Why do we need JSP if Servlets already exist?\n\nIf you write full HTML inside a Servlet, it becomes messy:\n\nout.println(\"<html>\");\nout.println(\"<body>\");\nout.println(\"<h1>Hello User</h1>\");\nout.println(\"</body></html>\");\n\n\nThis is extremely hard to maintain.\n\nSo JSP was created to make UI writing easier.\n\n✔ JSP = Best for HTML\n✔ Servlet = Best for logic / processing",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
