      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "🟦 4. Why JSP is converted into Servlet? (The Real Reason)\n\nBecause the server (Tomcat) only understands Java classes, not\nJSP syntax.\n\nSo Tomcat internally:\n\n✔ Reads JSP file\n✔ Converts it (compiles it) into a Java Servlet class\n✔ Then runs that servlet",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "🟦 4. Why JSP is converted into Servlet? (The Real Reason)\n\nBecause the server (Tomcat) only understands Java classes, not JSP syntax.\n\nSo Tomcat internally:\n\n✔ Reads JSP file\n✔ Converts it (compiles it) into a Java Servlet class\n✔ Then runs that servlet",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
