      "seed": 162546414,
      "version": 29,
      "versionNonce": 229665778,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1764395750154,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "🟦 6. Why does server convert JSP to Servlet?\n\nBecause Java code must run in a Java class, not inside HTML.\n\nServlet container (Tomcat) can only execute:\n\nJava classes\n\nCompiled .class files\n\nSo JSP must be converted → compiled → executed as Servlet.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "🟦 6. Why does server convert JSP to Servlet?\n\nBecause Java code must run in a Java class, not inside HTML.\n\nServlet container (Tomcat) can only execute:\n\nJava classes\n\nCompiled .class files\n\nSo JSP must be converted → compiled → executed as Servlet.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
