    {
      "id": "5U1ME0LLi9HMMRtAyIgEG",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 139.54077972632825,
      "y": 38957.36009846193,
      "width": 621.4609375,
      "height": 550,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bah",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 789789166,
      "version": 64,
      "versionNonce": 1467555246,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1764399239799,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "🟦 7. What the converted JSP Servlet actually looks like\n\nIf you write this JSP:\n\n<h1>Hello <%= name %></h1>\n\n\nTomcat converts it to:\n\npublic class Hello_jsp extends HttpServlet {\n    public void _jspService(HttpServletRequest req,\nHttpServletResponse resp) {\n        JspWriter out = resp.getWriter();\n        out.write(\"<h1>Hello \");\n        out.write(name);\n        out.write(\"</h1>\");\n    }\n}\n\n✔ Now Tomcat can execute it\n✔ Because now it's pure Java Servlet code\n✔ This is hidden from developers",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "🟦 7. What the converted JSP Servlet actually looks like\n\nIf you write this JSP:\n\n<h1>Hello <%= name %></h1>\n\n\nTomcat converts it to:\n\npublic class Hello_jsp extends HttpServlet {\n    public void _jspService(HttpServletRequest req, HttpServletResponse resp) {\n        JspWriter out = resp.getWriter();\n        out.write(\"<h1>Hello \");\n        out.write(name);\n        out.write(\"</h1>\");\n    }\n}\n\n✔ Now Tomcat can execute it\n✔ Because now it's pure Java Servlet code\n✔ This is hidden from developers",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
