      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1764401426071,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "✅ How to get the HttpServletRequest object in a Spring Boot API\n\nIn Spring Boot, you have three official ways to access the request\nobject:",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "✅ How to get the HttpServletRequest object in a Spring Boot API\n\nIn Spring Boot, you have three official ways to access the request object:",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "DssfidYwUhzFiefnwObs8",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -99.02044231319337,
      "y": 49050.4763108659,
      "width": 927.5932645694786,
      "height": 325,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bbi",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 261833518,
      "version": 111,
      "versionNonce": 1022233518,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1764401449739,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "🔵 1. Inject HttpServletRequest directly into your controller method (Most common)\n\n@GetMapping(\"/test\")\npublic String test(HttpServletRequest request) {\n    String ip = request.getRemoteAddr();\n    System.out.println(\"IP = \" + ip);\n    return \"ok\";\n}\n\n\n✔ Works automatically\n✔ Spring MVC passes the same request servlet object internally\n✔ No configuration needed",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "🔵 1. Inject HttpServletRequest directly into your controller method (Most common)\n\n@GetMapping(\"/test\")\npublic String test(HttpServletRequest request) {\n    String ip = request.getRemoteAddr();\n    System.out.println(\"IP = \" + ip);\n    return \"ok\";\n}\n\n\n✔ Works automatically\n✔ Spring MVC passes the same request servlet object internally\n✔ No configuration needed",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
