      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1764403828084,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Now we need to display this data also so we need to create a result.jsp page ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Now we need to display this data also so we need to create a result.jsp page ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "fLZha_eVk1cmZNLNE2sJp",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -121.95327925740776,
      "y": 54287.15277815861,
      "width": 960.8568605438301,
      "height": 600,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bc4",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 919281330,
      "version": 79,
      "versionNonce": 877572722,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1764403944162,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Display Data on Result Page\n \nHttpSession: Stores data that is available throughout a user's session.\n \nJSTL (JavaServer Pages Standard Tag Library): \n● Used for accessing attributes in JSP files. Example: ${result}. \n\nWe have a concept of session, so for a particular session, whatever you add in \nsession. \n\nAvailable for a particular session. \n\n\n1. Using the session object, add the result value inside the session.\n⇨ session.setAttribute(“result”,result); \n\n@RequestMapping(\"add\") \npublic String add(HttpServletRequest req, HttpSession session) { \nint num1 = Integer.parseInt(req.getParameter(\"num1\")); \nint num2 = Integer.parseInt(req.getParameter(\"num2\")); \nint result = num1 + num2; \nsession.setAttribute(\"result\", result); \nreturn \"result.jsp\"; \n}",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Display Data on Result Page\n \nHttpSession: Stores data that is available throughout a user's session.\n \nJSTL (JavaServer Pages Standard Tag Library): \n● Used for accessing attributes in JSP files. Example: ${result}. \n\nWe have a concept of session, so for a particular session, whatever you add in \nsession. \n\nAvailable for a particular session. \n\n\n1. Using the session object, add the result value inside the session.\n⇨ session.setAttribute(“result”,result); \n\n@RequestMapping(\"add\") \npublic String add(HttpServletRequest req, HttpSession session) { \nint num1 = Integer.parseInt(req.getParameter(\"num1\")); \nint num2 = Integer.parseInt(req.getParameter(\"num2\")); \nint result = num1 + num2; \nsession.setAttribute(\"result\", result); \nreturn \"result.jsp\"; \n}",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
