    {
      "id": "-fCksiIrmBv8xXdUMqIoR",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -80.79777863093659,
      "y": 55713.48128023402,
      "width": 868.8078482766438,
      "height": 425,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bcB",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2037757938,
      "version": 66,
      "versionNonce": 1096282290,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1764404063960,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "🟦 2. How They Work Internally\n✔ Spring MVC (Model)\n\nSpring gives you a Model object.\n\nmodel.addAttribute(\"name\", \"Shiv\");\nreturn \"home.jsp\";\n\n\nInternally Spring converts this to:\n\nrequest.setAttribute(\"name\", \"Shiv\");\n\n\n👉 So Model is just an abstraction over setAttribute().\n\nYou are not dealing with low-level HttpServletRequest.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "🟦 2. How They Work Internally\n✔ Spring MVC (Model)\n\nSpring gives you a Model object.\n\nmodel.addAttribute(\"name\", \"Shiv\");\nreturn \"home.jsp\";\n\n\nInternally Spring converts this to:\n\nrequest.setAttribute(\"name\", \"Shiv\");\n\n\n👉 So Model is just an abstraction over setAttribute().\n\nYou are not dealing with low-level HttpServletRequest.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
