      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1764404182717,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "🟩 3. Simple Example Comparison\n🔵 Using Spring MVC:\n    @GetMapping(\"/home\")\n    public String home(Model model) {\n        model.addAttribute(\"username\", \"Shiv\");\n        return \"home.jsp\";\n    }\n\n🔴 Using Servlet:\n    req.setAttribute(\"username\", \"Shiv\");\n    req.getRequestDispatcher(\"home.jsp\").forward(req, resp);\n\n\nBoth do the same thing → set a value that JSP will read:\n\nHello ${username}",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "🟩 3. Simple Example Comparison\n🔵 Using Spring MVC:\n    @GetMapping(\"/home\")\n    public String home(Model model) {\n        model.addAttribute(\"username\", \"Shiv\");\n        return \"home.jsp\";\n    }\n\n🔴 Using Servlet:\n    req.setAttribute(\"username\", \"Shiv\");\n    req.getRequestDispatcher(\"home.jsp\").forward(req, resp);\n\n\nBoth do the same thing → set a value that JSP will read:\n\nHello ${username}",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
