    {
      "id": "psE8gf9AjXauFhHLiLQ_B",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -92.79783907295291,
      "y": 58995.391899462506,
      "width": 583,
      "height": 550,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bcZ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 255269426,
      "version": 25,
      "versionNonce": 1579970542,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1764404303313,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "🟥 1. Very Important Rule\n\nThere are TWO types of attributes in web development:\n\n✔ request attributes\n\n→ live only for ONE request\n\n✔ session attributes\n\n→ live for the ENTIRE login/session\n\n🟦 2. Model in Spring MVC = Request Scope Only\n\nThis means:\n\nmodel.addAttribute(\"name\", \"Shiv\");\n\n\n⏳ Exists for ONE JSP render\n❌ Gone after the request ends\n❌ NOT stored for the user",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "🟥 1. Very Important Rule\n\nThere are TWO types of attributes in web development:\n\n✔ request attributes\n\n→ live only for ONE request\n\n✔ session attributes\n\n→ live for the ENTIRE login/session\n\n🟦 2. Model in Spring MVC = Request Scope Only\n\nThis means:\n\nmodel.addAttribute(\"name\", \"Shiv\");\n\n\n⏳ Exists for ONE JSP render\n❌ Gone after the request ends\n❌ NOT stored for the user",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
