    {
      "id": "SrxXKLpzSC0uTPZmo7gse",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 546.0841864685735,
      "y": 67012.60560437838,
      "width": 429,
      "height": 125,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bdL",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 130555314,
      "version": 212,
      "versionNonce": 189423794,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1764410324547,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Now here from HttpServletRequest req\nwe are taking the parameter which \nis the query parameter via getParameter\nwe can make this task a bit more \neasy using @RequestParam",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Now here from HttpServletRequest req\nwe are taking the parameter which \nis the query parameter via getParameter\nwe can make this task a bit more \neasy using @RequestParam",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "K8iPb0DlGryI66GYXAeJ9",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -294.59673701384986,
      "y": 67200.69041208585,
      "width": 1042.7339888276183,
      "height": 558.8535762092409,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bdM",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 149764078,
      "version": 106,
      "versionNonce": 1763189166,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1764410374930,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "RequestParam \n@RequestParam: \n● Maps query parameters or form data to method arguments. Example:\n \npublic String add(@RequestParam(\"num1\") int num1) {...} \n\n1. From the query parameter, we can take it. \n⇨ Using annotation @RequestParam() \n\n@RequestMapping(\"add\") \npublic String add(int num1, int num2, HttpSession session) { \nint result = num1 + num2 + 1; \nsession.setAttribute(\"result\", result); \nreturn \"result.jsp\"; \n} \n\n⇨ By default, inside the add method, the signatures work as \nadd(@RequestParam(“num1”) int num1, @RequestParam(“num2”) int \nnum2, HttpSession session).",
      "fontSize": 23.530676893020672,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "RequestParam \n@RequestParam: \n● Maps query parameters or form data to method arguments. Example:\n \npublic String add(@RequestParam(\"num1\") int num1) {...} \n\n1. From the query parameter, we can take it. \n⇨ Using annotation @RequestParam() \n\n@RequestMapping(\"add\") \npublic String add(int num1, int num2, HttpSession session) { \nint result = num1 + num2 + 1; \nsession.setAttribute(\"result\", result); \nreturn \"result.jsp\"; \n} \n\n⇨ By default, inside the add method, the signatures work as \nadd(@RequestParam(“num1”) int num1, @RequestParam(“num2”) int \nnum2, HttpSession session).",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
