      "seed": 2083387826,
      "version": 392,
      "versionNonce": 1080297134,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1764431152090,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "🟦 5. What is @ModelAttribute? (Most misunderstood)\n\n@ModelAttribute is used for:\n\n✔ Binding form data (HTML form → Java object)\n✔ Adding common attributes to all views\n    ->why we need ModelAttribute sometimes suppose \n      there are 20 input field value comming from \n      client instead of doing @RequestParam(input1),..........@RequestParam(input20)\n      we can use ModelAttribute define a class with those properties\n      and map that model-attribute parameter with class properties",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "🟦 5. What is @ModelAttribute? (Most misunderstood)\n\n@ModelAttribute is used for:\n\n✔ Binding form data (HTML form → Java object)\n✔ Adding common attributes to all views\n    ->why we need ModelAttribute sometimes suppose \n      there are 20 input field value comming from \n      client instead of doing @RequestParam(input1),..........@RequestParam(input20)\n      we can use ModelAttribute define a class with those properties\n      and map that model-attribute parameter with class properties",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "L0VwiMqZtCi2bfyb0247g",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -367.2499339162007,
      "y": 74183.00465955985,
      "width": 715,
      "height": 650,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bdt",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 681696946,
      "version": 73,
      "versionNonce": 724306158,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1764431216472,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "🟧 A) @ModelAttribute for Form Binding (MOST IMPORTANT USE)\n\nSuppose you submit a form:\n\n    <form action=\"/add\" method=\"post\">\n        <input name=\"name\">\n        <input name=\"age\">\n    </form>\n\n\nSpring can automatically fill a Java object with this form data:\n\n    @PostMapping(\"/add\")\n    public String addStudent(@ModelAttribute Student student) {\n        // Spring sets student.name and student.age automatically\n        service.save(student);\n        return \"success.jsp\";\n    }\n\n🟢 @ModelAttribute → creates object → fills it with request data\n\nNo need to use:\n\n    request.getParameter()\n\nor manually setting fields",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "🟧 A) @ModelAttribute for Form Binding (MOST IMPORTANT USE)\n\nSuppose you submit a form:\n\n    <form action=\"/add\" method=\"post\">\n        <input name=\"name\">\n        <input name=\"age\">\n    </form>\n\n\nSpring can automatically fill a Java object with this form data:\n\n    @PostMapping(\"/add\")\n    public String addStudent(@ModelAttribute Student student) {\n        // Spring sets student.name and student.age automatically\n        service.save(student);\n        return \"success.jsp\";\n    }\n\n🟢 @ModelAttribute → creates object → fills it with request data\n\nNo need to use:\n\n    request.getParameter()\n\nor manually setting fields",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
