    {
      "id": "IA4aqy8ZI9GdgDQlWCZtN",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -389.8837577774834,
      "y": 77427.96442766399,
      "width": 726,
      "height": 125,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "beC",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 968493554,
      "version": 37,
      "versionNonce": 866617134,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1764431598828,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Yes — you MUST create the class first before using\n@ModelAttribute.\nSpring cannot magically guess what fields your form will have.\nSo you always need a Java POJO (model class) that matches the form\nfields.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Yes — you MUST create the class first before using @ModelAttribute.\nSpring cannot magically guess what fields your form will have.\nSo you always need a Java POJO (model class) that matches the form fields.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "XUNd993K2Q8SOGgBwBraf",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -396.4425315318184,
      "y": 77583.76209666226,
      "width": 561,
      "height": 575,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "beD",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1179174450,
      "version": 83,
      "versionNonce": 2129722094,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1764431653752,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "✅ 1. Why do we need a class for @ModelAttribute?\n\nBecause Spring does this internally:\n\nCreate object → Fill fields → Give it to controller\n\n\nTo do that, Spring needs a real class with:\n\n->fields\n\n->getters/setters\n\na no-argument constructor\n\nExample:\n\n    public class Student {\n        private String name;\n        private int age;\n    \n        // MUST: getters + setters\n    }",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "✅ 1. Why do we need a class for @ModelAttribute?\n\nBecause Spring does this internally:\n\nCreate object → Fill fields → Give it to controller\n\n\nTo do that, Spring needs a real class with:\n\n->fields\n\n->getters/setters\n\na no-argument constructor\n\nExample:\n\n    public class Student {\n        private String name;\n        private int age;\n    \n        // MUST: getters + setters\n    }",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "w-rNkIkNftjFv14LyuefD",
