    {
      "id": "iL9kWUNV51KUT-ya6mZB0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -411.3849063091471,
      "y": 78628.04989098579,
      "width": 794.8582937956686,
      "height": 550,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "beH",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1047941938,
      "version": 174,
      "versionNonce": 1563208238,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1764431738091,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "🟦 2. What does @ModelAttribute actually do?\n\nIf your form contains:\n\n    <input name=\"name\">\n    <input name=\"age\">\n\n\nAnd your controller has:\n\n    @PostMapping(\"/add\")\n    public String add(@ModelAttribute Student student) { … }\n\n\nSpring performs:\n\n    Student student = new Student();\n    student.setName(req.getParameter(\"name\"));\n    student.setAge(Integer.parseInt(req.getParameter(\"age\")));\n    \n\nThen passes the filled object to your method.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "🟦 2. What does @ModelAttribute actually do?\n\nIf your form contains:\n\n    <input name=\"name\">\n    <input name=\"age\">\n\n\nAnd your controller has:\n\n    @PostMapping(\"/add\")\n    public String add(@ModelAttribute Student student) { … }\n\n\nSpring performs:\n\n    Student student = new Student();\n    student.setName(req.getParameter(\"name\"));\n    student.setAge(Integer.parseInt(req.getParameter(\"age\")));\n    \n\nThen passes the filled object to your method.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
