    {
      "id": "T9m4f-RV-2kKBGKF6-B3B",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -422.730410706282,
      "y": 79637.58837731405,
      "width": 566.4609375,
      "height": 425,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "beN",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 196174194,
      "version": 65,
      "versionNonce": 1478282606,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1764431796945,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "🟥 3. What happens if the class does NOT exist?\n\nYou get errors like:\n\n->\"Cannot resolve class\"\n\n->\"Failed to instantiate ModelAttribute\"\n\n->\"No default constructor present\"\n\nBecause Spring cannot create the object.\n\n🟩 4. So the rule is:\n✔ If you want to bind form data → YES create class\n✔ The class must have fields matching input names\n✔ Must have getters & setters\n✔ Must have a no-arg constructor (default)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "🟥 3. What happens if the class does NOT exist?\n\nYou get errors like:\n\n->\"Cannot resolve class\"\n\n->\"Failed to instantiate ModelAttribute\"\n\n->\"No default constructor present\"\n\nBecause Spring cannot create the object.\n\n🟩 4. So the rule is:\n✔ If you want to bind form data → YES create class\n✔ The class must have fields matching input names\n✔ Must have getters & setters\n✔ Must have a no-arg constructor (default)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
