      "seed": 42950510,
      "version": 39,
      "versionNonce": 593361838,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1764431915079,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "🟨 6. Can we use ModelAttribute without a class?\n\nYes, but only for single values:\n\n    @PostMapping(\"/add\")\n    public String addStudent(@ModelAttribute(\"name\") String name)\n{ … }\n\n\nBut this is rare.\n@ModelAttribute is MOSTLY used with classes.\n\n⭐ Final Answer\n✔ YES, you must create the class first.\n\n@ModelAttribute needs an object to bind form data into.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "🟨 6. Can we use ModelAttribute without a class?\n\nYes, but only for single values:\n\n    @PostMapping(\"/add\")\n    public String addStudent(@ModelAttribute(\"name\") String name) { … }\n\n\nBut this is rare.\n@ModelAttribute is MOSTLY used with classes.\n\n⭐ Final Answer\n✔ YES, you must create the class first.\n\n@ModelAttribute needs an object to bind form data into.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
